<%# KI-Pakete P4b (doc/ki_pakete_p4_plan.md §4): the consequence dialog that has
    to precede a lane-moving package switch.

    A PAGE and not a modal, deliberately. Three reasons, in order of weight:
      * E7 wants the estimate computed once, when the dialog opens — a panel on
        #show would run its four aggregate queries on every visit to the settings
        page, and a modal per card would put N of them into one render.
      * It is the heaviest decision this screen offers (jurisdiction, a metered
        re-embedding of the whole corpus, a search index that rebuilds for
        minutes to hours). A dismissible overlay is the wrong weight for it.
      * It is fully assertable from a request spec, with no Capybara blindness
        inside turbo_stream templates and no JS at all.

    The order below is the order the customer decides in: what changes legally,
    then what it costs, then whether the quota covers it, then what the search
    does meanwhile. %>
<div class="max-w-3xl">
  <%= render 'organisations/shared/ai_area_header', title: t('views.organisations.ai_overview.pages.switch') %>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-lg font-bold text-cream-900">
    <i class="bi bi-arrow-left-right mr-2"></i>
    <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.title') %>
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-cream-800">
    <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.intro',
          target: @target_package&.name ||
                  t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.title')) %>
  </p>

  <%# 1 — what changes legally. The two claims side by side, each with the
      restricting addendum the card shows, so the comparison reads in the same
      words the customer chose the package in. %>
  <div class="mt-6 border-2 border-ink rounded-lg bg-surface-raised p-4 shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#000000]">
    <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-cream-900 uppercase tracking-wide">
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.legal_heading') %>
    </h3>

    <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <% [[t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.side_today'), @current_package,
           @current_jurisdiction, @current_training, @current_retention],
          [t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.side_after'), @target_package,
           @target_jurisdiction, @target_training, @target_retention]].each do |label, package, jurisdiction, training_usage, retention| %>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-bold text-cream-700 uppercase tracking-wide"><%= label %></p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold text-cream-900">
            <%= package&.name || t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.title') %>
          </p>
          <%# Since T7 the same two badges as on the card, in the same order:
              the comparison should read in exactly the words in which the
              customer chose the package. %>
          <p class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <%= render 'organisations/ai_settings/jurisdiction_badge', jurisdiction: jurisdiction %>
            <%= render 'organisations/ai_settings/training_badge', training_usage: training_usage %>
          </p>
          <%# The third occurrence came with T5 (the card now carries three such
              addenda), so the idiom was extracted here. The trigger was already
              noted at this spot. `fallback` is the only difference from the card:
              "nichts eingestuft" is a statement in a COMPARISON, on the card it
              stays silent. %>
          <%= render 'organisations/ai_settings/claim_note',
                     scope: 'views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.jurisdiction_notes',
                     value: jurisdiction,
                     fallback: t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.jurisdiction_unstated') %>

          <%# Training addendum and retention sentence WITHOUT a fallback: if a
              side says nothing about it, it stays silent here too. The reason is
              in the jurisdiction line above: self_hosted and "Eigene
              Konfiguration" are already explained there, a second vague sentence
              would be noise. %>
          <%= render 'organisations/ai_settings/claim_note',
                     scope: 'views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.training_notes',
                     value: training_usage %>
          <% retention_policy, retention_days = retention %>
          <%= render 'organisations/ai_settings/claim_note',
                     scope: 'views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.retention_notes',
                     value: retention_policy,
                     args: retention_days ? { count: retention_days } : {} %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%# The one-line verdict. Four cases rather than three: a package that claims
        nothing must not be reported as an improvement OR as a deterioration
        (see AiSettingsController#jurisdiction_change). %>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-bold text-cream-900">
      <%= t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.jurisdiction_change.#{@jurisdiction_change}") %>
    </p>

    <%# T7: the same construction, one axis deeper. nil means NO line: if either
        side says nothing about training, there is nothing to compare, and the
        jurisdiction line above already explains why (self_hosted or "Eigene
        Konfiguration"). This case is deliberately NOT turned into a sentence:
        that was exactly the defect the #437 review removed from the neighbouring
        method four times. %>
    <% if @training_change %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-bold text-cream-900">
        <%= t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.training_change.#{@training_change}") %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# The three blocks below exist exactly when there is a migration to describe.
      Asked as "did the controller compute the consequences?" rather than as a
      second `ai_enabled?` read: #load_switch_consequences already decides that,
      and a view re-deciding it is how the page and the queries behind it drift
      into disagreeing about which case this is. @estimate is nil precisely when
      the AI opt-in is off — see the else branch. %>
  <% if @estimate %>
    <%# 2 — the price. An ESTIMATE and labelled as one (E7): the token count is a
        characters/4 rule of thumb, and the whole corpus is counted although the
        run skips what the target space already holds. Both errors point the same
        way — the real run tends to be smaller. %>
    <div class="mt-4 border border-cream-300 rounded-lg bg-surface-raised p-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-cream-900 uppercase tracking-wide">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.cost_heading') %>
      </h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-cream-800 tabular-nums">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.cost_estimate',
              records: number_with_delimiter(@estimate.records),
              credits: number_with_delimiter(@estimate.credits)) %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-cream-700">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.cost_estimate_hint') %>
      </p>
    </div>

    <%# 3 — the quota pre-check. §9's first hard precondition, and the reason this
        dialog had to exist before the card doors could open: the gate fires ONCE,
        at the provider build, so a run that starts inside the budget keeps going
        until the corpus is done — and can take chat AND semantic search down with
        it for the rest of the month.

        Two different faults, two different texts:
          * already exhausted → the run cannot start at all. It is not lost:
            ReindexOrganisationJob logs "switch paused" and P4d's watcher picks it
            up once the budget rolls over.
          * estimate above what is left → the run WILL start and WILL overshoot.

        All of it hangs on @quota_relevant first. The gate that stops a run asks the
        CREDENTIAL of the target lane, not the organisation — `included_in_quota`
        defaults to false, so for a lane nobody flagged, every branch below would
        describe a block that cannot fire (#437 review, blocker 1). Saying nothing is
        then the honest answer: the run still costs the OPERATOR, and that is not
        this customer's decision to weigh. %>
    <% if !@quota_relevant %>
    <% elsif @quota_exhausted %>
      <div class="mt-4 border border-red-300 rounded-lg bg-red-50 p-4">
        <p class="text-sm font-bold text-red-900">
          <i class="bi bi-x-octagon mr-1"></i><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.quota_exhausted_title') %>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-red-800"><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.quota_exhausted_body') %></p>
      </div>
    <% elsif @quota_shortfall.positive? %>
      <div class="mt-4 border border-amber-300 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 p-4">
        <p class="text-sm font-bold text-amber-900">
          <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle mr-1"></i><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.quota_short_title') %>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-amber-800 tabular-nums">
          <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.quota_short_body',
                remaining: number_with_delimiter(@quota.remaining),
                planned: number_with_delimiter(@quota_planned),
                shortfall: number_with_delimiter(@quota_shortfall)) %>
        </p>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <div class="mt-4 border border-cream-300 rounded-lg bg-surface-raised p-4">
        <p class="text-sm text-cream-800 tabular-nums">
          <i class="bi bi-speedometer2 mr-1"></i>
          <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.quota_covered',
                remaining: number_with_delimiter(@quota.remaining)) %>
        </p>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <%# 4 — what the search does meanwhile (E3, decided as A: name the gap rather
        than write into both spaces).

        TWO different promises, because two different org states exist:
          * with a space pointer — the old index keeps serving until the new one is
            complete, so the BESTAND stays findable throughout; only content created
            during the window is not, and that gets said out loud.
          * WITHOUT one — Factory.embedding_space_for(:active) falls back to the
            CONFIGURED triple, so reads move onto the new, empty space the moment the
            write lands: search and RAG chat return nothing until the rebuild is done.
            Printing the reassuring text there is a promise the code does not keep
            (#437 review, blocker 2). The state is reachable because the pointer is
            nullable and #431's backfill is fail-soft. %>
    <div class="mt-4 border rounded-lg p-4 <%= @search_outcome == :search_body ? 'border-cream-300 bg-cream-100' : 'border-amber-300 bg-amber-50' %>">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-cream-900 uppercase tracking-wide">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.search_heading') %>
      </h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-cream-800">
        <%= t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.#{@search_outcome}") %>
      </p>
      <%# WHO receives the search input, before and after. The "today" side is the
          P5 disclosure's own answer — the space that actually SERVES, not the
          configured lane — so this page cannot name a different recipient than
          the Art. 13 notice on the chat page does for the same moment. %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-cream-800">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.search_recipients',
              today: @disclosure.embedding_provider_label, after: @target_search_label) %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-cream-800"><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.search_gap') %></p>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <%# The org's AI opt-in is off — the DB default, so this is the common case.
        Actors::SelectAiPackage#enqueue_jobs returns early for such an org: no
        corpus is re-embedded, nothing is charged, nothing is transmitted. A price
        and a rebuild notice here would describe events that cannot happen. %>
    <div class="mt-4 border border-cream-300 rounded-lg bg-cream-100 p-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-cream-800"><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.ai_disabled_note') %></p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
    <%# The SAME write the card used to fire directly, with the same blank-id
        convention for the way back (E1-C) — the dialog is a step in front of it,
        not a second code path. %>
    <%= render Neo::Buttons::ButtonComponent.new(
      variant: :primary,
      size: :medium,
      icon: "arrow-left-right",
      form: { action: select_package_organisation_ai_settings_path(@organisation),
              method: :post,
              params: { ai_package_id: @target_package&.id.to_s } }
    ) do %>
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.confirm_button') %>
    <% end %>

    <%= render Neo::Buttons::ButtonComponent.new(
      variant: :secondary,
      size: :medium,
      url: organisation_ai_settings_path(@organisation, package_mode: @package_mode)
    ) do %>
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.switch.cancel_button') %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
